# Legacy paths stay above the host rules. They are host-agnostic and relative,
# so an old URL still maps to its new path. The host rules use :splat and must
# not replace these with a homepage redirect. The 404 catch-all stays last.
/services/weekly-pool-service/ /services/regular-pool-maintenance/ 301
/services/pool-equipment-repair/ /services/pool-repair/ 301
/services/bead-blasting/ /services/pool-tile-cleaning/ 301
/services/green-to-clean/ /services/green-pool-cleanup/ 301
/blog/winterizing-your-pool-tips-for/ /blog/ 301
/blog/winterizing-your-pool-tips-for /blog/ 301

# Canonical origin is https://calvalleypools.com/ (non-www HTTPS).
# With force HTTPS, Netlify upgrades HTTP to HTTPS on the SAME host before
# these rules (HSTS). A rule from http://www straight to the apex never runs.
# Same-host HTTP rules cover force-HTTPS being off; the HTTPS www rule is the
# hop that reaches the apex. ! forces the redirect when the homepage file exists.
http://calvalleypools.com/* https://calvalleypools.com/:splat 301!
http://www.calvalleypools.com/* https://www.calvalleypools.com/:splat 301!
https://www.calvalleypools.com/* https://calvalleypools.com/:splat 301!

